   "date": "2013-06-28",
   "stage_hint": null,
   "brief": "The Grape and Wine Legislation Amendment Bill creates the Australian Grape and Wine Authority from 1 July 2014, merging the Grape and Wine Research and Development Corporation and Wine Australia Corporation to improve industry efficiency, while the Rural Research and Development Legislation Amendment Bill allows statutory research and development corporations to undertake marketing and match voluntary contributions. The Homelessness Bill sets a target to halve homelessness by 2020 and provide supported accommodation for all rough sleepers, with a revised definition recognising those in crisis accommodation or unsafe homes."
